{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Smv86UxDFQ4CAaLoVZQEmX","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"Audio processor port definition for domain layer.\n     2→\n     3→Defines the interface for audio processing operations.\n     4→\"\"\"\n     5→\n     6→from pathlib import Path\n     7→from typing import Protocol\n     8→\n     9→from core.domain.value_objects.audio_result import AudioResult\n    10→from core.domain.value_objects.tone_config import ToneConfig\n    11→from core.domain.value_objects.waveform_data import WaveformData\n    12→\n    13→\n    14→class AudioProcessor(Protocol):\n    15→    \"\"\"Protocol for audio processing operations.\n    16→\n    17→    This port defines the interface that the domain layer expects\n    18→    from audio processing implementations. The actual implementation\n    19→    lives in libs/audio.\n    20→    \"\"\"\n    21→\n    22→    async def process_di_track(\n    23→        self,\n    24→        input_path: Path,\n    25→        output_path: Path,\n    26→        config: ToneConfig,\n    27→    ) -> AudioResult:\n    28→        \"\"\"Process a DI track through a tone configuration.\n    29→\n    30→        Args:\n    31→            input_path: Path to the input DI audio file\n    32→            output_path: Path for the processed output file\n    33→            config: Tone processing configuration\n    34→\n    35→        Returns:\n    36→            AudioResult with processing metadata\n    37→\n    38→        Raises:\n    39→            ProcessingError: If processing fails\n    40→        \"\"\"\n    41→        ...\n    42→\n    43→    async def extract_waveform(\n    44→        self,\n    45→        audio_path: Path,\n    46→        *,\n    47→        num_peaks: int = 200,\n    48→    ) -> WaveformData:\n    49→        \"\"\"Extract waveform visualization data from audio.\n    50→\n    51→        Args:\n    52→            audio_path: Path to the audio file\n    53→          